; Timeline player: drives 13 consecutive pins (GP10-GP22) from a stream of
; (pin levels, duration) words, fed continuously by DMA (timeline_output.cpp).
;
; Word layout (see src/core/timeline.h):
;   bits 0..12   level of each pin, bit 0 = the lowest pin
;   bits 13..31  loop count
; The OSR shifts right with autopull at 32 bits, so the levels come out first.
;
; Timing per word: `out pins` (1) + `out x` (1) + `jmp x--` executed count+1
; times = count + 3 cycles. All 13 pins change together on the first
; instruction of each word. As long as DMA keeps the FIFO from running empty,
; autopull never stalls and every word is cycle exact.

.program timeline

.wrap_target
    out pins, 13        ; set all pin levels for this word
    out x, 19           ; load the duration
delay:
    jmp x-- delay
.wrap
